  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This book is a visual mediation on war and racism. In collage and poetry Bisa Washington summons old magic to help comprehend the presistence of war and hate in South Africa. The book opens with a page full of skulls and the text: "In the event anyone disappears! what will we do now? Will we sing, shout, scream the epitaphs, as we carry the bodies away? What will we/you do now that Malcolm, Martin, Amilacar, Lumumba, Nelson, and my cousin who you don't even know is dead or immobilized?"--Visual Studies Workshop website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
